TEXT 712 1080 Left 2 ;.tran 0 330m 300m
TEXT -840 -152 Left 2 ;2. Converting to Dual Voltage Supply\nThe original circuit is designed for a single supply where $V_{ss}$ is $0V$ (Ground). \nTo run this on a dual supply (e.g., $+V$ and $-V$):\nOp-Amps (A1, A2): Connect pin 8 to $+V$ and pin 4 to $-V$.\n555 Timer: Connect pin 8 to $+V$. Crucially, pin 1 ($V_{ss}/GND$) should stay connected to your system Ground ($0V$), not $-V$.\nMost standard 555 models aren't designed to have their ground pin swing below $0V$ relative to the control pins without extra biasing.\nGrounding: Any point in the original diagram connected to the $V_{ss}$ line should be connected to your common $0V$ Ground.
TEXT 1088 936 Left 2 ;amplitude knob
TEXT 5096 72 Left 2 !.lib ad633.sub
TEXT 5944 -128 Left 2 !.options gminsteps=0 reltol=1e-3 abstol=1e-6 vntol=1e-3 method=gear
TEXT 2536 2248 Left 2 ;.tran 0 11m 10m startup
TEXT 2192 32 Left 2 !.options method=gear solver=Alternate\n.options abstol=1e-12 reltol=0.001 vntol=1e-06
